- Editor of one value of a `view.tree` property, dispatching on the shape of the
- value and recursing into composite ones.
-
- Port of `hyoo_studio_value` and its six sub editors, plus a seventh the studio
- has no equivalent of: the wire `=` of section 1. Deviations are marked at their
- place.
-
- Every class here derives from something OUTSIDE this file, and that is a rule,
- not a coincidence. Declarations of a `view.tree` are emitted before the
- handwritten bodies of the same module, so a class inheriting a neighbour from
- this very file would extend the version without its `.view.ts` methods — half
- the behaviour gone, nothing reported. Studio can afford `hyoo_studio_value_object
- hyoo_studio_value_dict` because there the two live in separate modules.
- List, dictionary and object are therefore one class with two flags rather than
- three classes in a chain.
- @see ../../../../ARCHITECTURE.md section 3
$bog_vmap_app_inspect_value $mol_view
	- The value node. Writing serializes it back into the document.
	tree? $mol_tree2_empty
	- Property names of the class this value belongs to, offered as binding targets.
	binds /string
	- Nodes a wire may start from, by name, each carrying the class it is declared
	- with and the ports that class has. Both ends of a wire are picked out of this
	- one map, so neither end can be spelled by hand into something that does not
	- exist.
	nodes *
	- Why the last edit was refused, empty while there is nothing to say.
	-
	- A refusal has to be legible, and on its own it is not. `$mol_string` catches
	- what a setter throws and puts the message into `setCustomValidity`
	- (`mol/string/string.view.ts:36`), which the browser shows on form submit and
	- nowhere else. In a form that is never submitted the value silently stays out
	- of the document and the field keeps the text nobody accepted — the document
	- is safe and the person is lost.
	alarm? \
	sub <= editors /$mol_view
	Alarm $mol_view sub / <= alarm
	- Every editor is declared, one is rendered. Studio picks the same way and then
	- copies the context onto the chosen instance field by field
	- (`obj.tree = …`, `obj.props_of = …`). Here the context arrives through
	- ordinary bindings instead, so the wiring is visible in the declaration and
	- type checked, and swapping the shape of a value cannot leave an editor
	- holding a stale accessor.
