- Camera lives here: `camera_shift` is a screen-pixel vector, `camera_zoom` an
- isotropic scalar. $mol_touch drives both from pointer, wheel and pinch.
$bog_vmap_app_pane $mol_view
	- Absolute address of the `web.js` of the sandbox module. The frame has no
	- address of its own, so the markup it is raised from names the bundle itself,
	- and a relative path would have nothing to resolve against in an opaque origin.
	scene_bundle \
	- Whole document of the frame, built out of `scene_bundle` in `pane.view.ts`.
	scene_html \
	- Absolute address of the `web.js` of the donor pack, sent down as `pack_set`.
	- Part of the key of the frame as well: a realm cannot unload a bundle, so a
	- different pack has to be a different frame, see section 5.
	pack_uri \
	doc_src \
	doc_css \
	- Canvas placement of free parts, world coordinates keyed by property name.
	- Never joined with `doc_css`: that one is the document, this one is the desk.
	- Two way: dragging a node on the canvas writes here.
	spots? *
	- Property name of the picked node, `null` when nothing is picked.
	selected? null
	doc_js *
	doc_root \
	- Sources of the land libraries, compiled by the scene before the document.
	- On the bridge and not in `scene_uri`: a change of lands is a recompile, a
	- change of pack is a reload, see section 5.
	libs /$bog_vmap_bridge_part
	- Whether the overlay may be cut open under the picked part. The host turns
	- this off while something is carried from the palette: that gesture has no
	- pointer capture, so a release over the hole would land in the frame and the
	- host would never hear of the drop.
	hole_allowed true
	- Wires of the document and the wirable ports of each part's class, from the
	- owner. The pane draws them and writes back through the two events below; it
	- never touches the document itself.
	wires /$bog_vmap_lang_link
	part_ports* /$bog_vmap_app_wire_port
	link_add? null
	link_drop? null
	- Nodes that carry a `sub` of their own: an artboard, and anything laid out by
	- tree inside one. A drop inside one of these goes into the tree at a position,
	- see section 8; a drop anywhere else lands on the canvas by coordinates.
	containers /string
	- `flexDirection` the node declares, empty when it declares none. From the
	- document, which the host owns, and so a statement rather than a guess: the
	- boxes of the children say nothing when there are fewer than two of them.
	axis* \
	- A node put into the tree of a container. The pane owns the geometry of the
	- gesture and asks the owner to write the document, never writing it itself.
	tree_move? null
	- Labels of the wires on screen, by wire name, as the scene reports them.
	values? *
	- Handshakes seen from ONE frame, keyed by the key of that frame. A fresh frame
	- has said nothing yet, and reads zero here without anybody having to remember
	- to clear anything.
	handshake*? 0
	ready false
	- The scene owes an answer to something we sent and has stopped answering.
	- Set by the watchdog, cleared by the next message from the scene.
	stalled? false
	error_at*? \
	- Node the failure of a channel belongs to, empty when the scene could not
	- attribute it. Kept apart from the text so that the strip and the mark on the
	- canvas read the same report without either parsing the other's sentence.
	error_node*? \
	error \
	isolation \
	camera_shift? $mol_vector_2d<number> /
		0
		0
	camera_zoom? 1
	- Which frame is live. Bumped by `scene_restart`: a new key is a new frame
	- element, so a stuck scene is replaced rather than talked to. The address of
	- the pack goes into the key beside it, see `scene_key`.
	scene_generation? 0
	Scene* $bog_vmap_app_pane_frame
		html <= scene_html
	sub /
		<= Overlay $bog_vmap_app_pane_overlay
			style <= overlay_style *
			frame_showed <= frame_showed false
